//
// Conduit Path C end-to-end regression for the
// `effectiveRepeat = std::max(channelDmaRepeat, outerRepeat)`
// double-counting bug at ConduitToDMALower.cpp (~line 1300).
//
// IR-level companion (FileCheck on Pass C output, no aiecc):
//   test/Dialect/Conduit/passc_effective_repeat_no_double_count.mlir
//
// Bug shape (full description in companion aie.mlir header): IRON-emitted
// shim S2MM configures with explicit {repeat_count = 1} + a 4-dim BD
// whose outer dim has <size = 2, stride > 0> (a real iteration).  Pre-fix
// Pass C emitted push-queue repeat_count = max(1, 2) = 2 onto the
// post-Pass-C configure_task; firmware MULTIPLIES BD outer (=2) and
// push-queue (=2), so the BD over-fired 4× per configure instead of the
// intended 2.  Each over-fire pair re-walked the BD's offsets [0, 1024B]
// and OVERWROTE the first walk's data.
//
// Post-fix expected: PASS on npu2 with byte-exact output[i] == i / 256
// for the 1024-int output buffer (4 contiguous 256-i32 quarters holding
// the broadcast values 0, 1, 2, 3 respectively).
//
// Pre-fix shape: test.cpp catches via mismatch and prints the exact
// pre-fix shape it sees (output quarters holding 2, 3, 6, 7), so
// regressions of this specific bug are identified by name in the failure
// output.
//
// Why ONLY a conduit run (no stateful counterpart): the bug is in Pass C
// (--conduit-to-dma).  Stateful does not run Pass C, so this exact
// over-fire codepath is unreachable on stateful — a stateful run would
// just exercise IRON's pre-existing BD lowering, which is unaffected.
// Pinning the post-fix invariant in conduit alone is sufficient and
// keeps the smoke narrow to the transform under fix (per amendment Q2:
// "narrows to transform under fix — failures unambiguously implicate
// Pass C → AIE lowering + HW exec").
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai
//
// RUN: cp %S/aie.mlir aie_arch.mlir
// RUN: %run_on_npu2% sed 's/NPUDEVICE/npu2_1col/g' -i aie_arch.mlir
// RUN: %run_on_npu2% %python aiecc.py --no-aiesim --aie-generate-xclbin --aie-generate-npu-insts --no-compile-host --use-conduit --xclbin-name=aie.xclbin --npu-insts-name=insts.bin aie_arch.mlir
// RUN: %run_on_npu2% clang %S/test.cpp -o test.exe -std=c++17 -Wall %xrt_flags -lrt -lstdc++ %test_utils_flags
// RUN: %run_on_npu2% ./test.exe -x aie.xclbin -k MLIR_AIE -i insts.bin
